<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Product Development Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>

                ```
                <p>
                    Product development can become difficult when requirements change frequently,
                    teams are not aligned, technical dependencies are overlooked, or development
                    priorities are not clearly defined. Identifying these challenges early can
                    improve delivery efficiency and product quality.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Changing Requirements:</b> Customer expectations and business priorities
                    can change during development. Maintaining a prioritized backlog and clear
                    product roadmap helps teams respond without losing overall direction.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Unclear Scope:</b> Poorly defined scope can result in unnecessary features,
                    delays, and increased development costs. Clear requirements and feature
                    prioritization help teams remain focused.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Communication Gaps:</b> Miscommunication between business, design,
                    development, and testing teams can create rework. Regular collaboration
                    and clear documentation help maintain alignment.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Technical Dependencies:</b> Integrations, third-party services, legacy
                    systems, and infrastructure requirements can affect delivery timelines.
                    Identifying dependencies early allows teams to plan them appropriately.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Quality Issues:</b> Delaying testing until the end of development can
                    make defects expensive and time-consuming to resolve. Continuous testing
                    throughout development helps improve product quality.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant product development challenges image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
