                ```
                <p>
                    Clear requirements provide a common understanding between product
                    stakeholders and development teams. Requirements should explain what
                    the product needs to accomplish, who will use it, and what outcomes
                    are expected.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Development planning then converts these requirements into manageable
                    activities, milestones, releases, and technical tasks. Teams can
                    prioritize work according to business impact, customer value,
                    dependencies, and development effort.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Define functional and non-functional requirements.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Break larger requirements into manageable development tasks.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Identify technical dependencies and potential delivery risks.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Establish milestones and release priorities.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

