                ```
                <p>
                    Agile product development enables teams to deliver product capabilities
                    incrementally rather than waiting until the entire product is completed.
                    Development work can be organized into manageable iterations with clearly
                    defined objectives and deliverables.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Iterative delivery allows teams to collect feedback earlier, identify
                    technical or usability issues sooner, and adjust priorities as new
                    information becomes available. This approach can improve transparency
                    and help organizations respond to changing customer and business needs.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Regular planning, development reviews, testing, demonstrations, and
                    retrospectives help teams continuously improve their delivery process
                    while keeping the product roadmap aligned with business objectives.
