                <h3><b>Testing, Quality Assurance and Product Validation</b></h3>

                ```
                <p>
                    Quality assurance is an important part of product development because
                    customers expect products to be reliable, secure, responsive, and easy
                    to use. Testing should be integrated into the development lifecycle
                    rather than being performed only before the final release.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Functional testing verifies that features behave according to requirements,
                    while integration testing evaluates interactions between different systems
                    and services. Performance and security testing can identify additional
                    risks that may affect the overall product experience.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Validate product functionality against defined requirements.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Test integrations between internal and external systems.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Identify usability and performance issues before release.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Verify product reliability across supported environments.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

